.²1 A particle added to the present tense of verbs (or to present participles)
 and giving them the sense of the past tense; {#BAsurako nAma siMhaH prativasati#}
 {#sma#} <ls>Pt. 1</ls>; {#krIRanti sma prARamUlyEryaSAMsi#} <ls>Śi. 18. 15</ls>.
.²2 A pleonastic particle (generally added to the prohibitive particle
 {#mA#} <ab>q. v.</ab>); {#BarturviprakftApi rozaRatayA mAsma pratIpaM gamaH#} <ls>Ś. 4. 18</ls>;
 {#mAsma sImantinI kAcijjanayet putramIdfSam#} <ls>H. 2. 7</ls>.
.²3 A particle giving a sense of ‘ever’, ‘always’ or ‘indeed’, ‘verily’
 and like; {#uvAca viprAH pratinandya pArTivaM mudA munInAM sadasi sma#}
 {#SfRvatAm#} <ls>Bhāg. 8. 1. 33</ls>.
